        # uses, shell.cyr:460-463). 1.46.x #2: the child stays at state=3 (elf_load_from_file
        # leaves it NOT-ready) for the WHOLE foreground run — it is entered out-of-band via
        # exec_and_wait/enter_ring3 below (never via sched), then exit#0 flips it state=0. Never
        # being state==1 means no woken AP can sched-pick (double-run) it; exec_and_wait's pin is
        # the second guard. So there is deliberately NO proc_set_state(cpid,1) on this path.
