        # fb_shadow != 0) or paint via fb_putc instead.
        # rect is CLIPPED to the FB bounds (off-screen rows/cols dropped), so both
        # the src reads and the FB writes are provably in range. Pixels copy RAW (no
        # format conversion) — the caller supplies fbinfo's reported byte order. The
        # write goes straight to fb_phys, EXACTLY as fb_putc does from ring-3 stdout
        # (the proven path): the handler runs in the same syscall context that already
        # both reads user buffers (uname/sysinfo) and writes fb_phys (write#1→fb_putc),
